onstration sport, in 1936 and " [:a {:href "/editions/37/sports/IST"} "1964"] ". In 1936, there were eight different events, with six for men (three international and three national) and two national events for women. Little is known about the details of the various events. Admission to the events was free. In the distance events, each competitor had three attempts with the best attempt counting. In the target events, each competitor had five shots at a house with a target, scoring from 1-9 points. The 1936 events were held on the " [:a {:href "/venues/38"} "Rießersee"] ", a lake, with several of the events held under less than ideal conditions, because of snow. The competition was organized by Josef Dötsch, a leading proponent of the sport in Germany."] "\n\n"] "\n\n\n" [:h2 {} "Non-medal events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/905038"} "Target Shooting (International), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic (non-medal)"] "\n" [:td {} "10 February 1936"] "\n" [:td {} "12"] "\n" [:td {} "3"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/905069"} "Target Shooting (National), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic (non-medal)"] "\n" [:td {} " 9 February 1936"] "\n" [:td {} "14"] "\n" [:td {} "1"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/905039"} "Distance Shooting (International), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic (non-medal)"] "\n" [:td {} " 9 February 1936"] "\n" [:td {} "12"] "\n" [:td {} "3"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/905070"} "Distance Shooting (National), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic (non-medal)"] "\n" [:td {} "10 February 1936"] "\n" [:td {} "14"] "\n" [:td {} "1"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/905040"} "Team (International), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic (non-medal)"] "\n" [:td {} " 9 February 